WEBVTT

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:48.450
"Notice: Because of Itsuki Otori's withdrawal from the Kao Council,
Team Otori has been demoted to a regular team."

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.330
Otori withdrew...?

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:55.080
"Demoted to a regular team"...
We didn't hear anything about that!

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.830
What's going on?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.540
I was confused.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:10.250
Otori and his smile that
I had just seen yesterday...

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.950
...were starting to fade and grow blurry.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.250
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:33.580
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:40.750
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:48.580
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.080
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.620
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:04.870
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:11.120
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.160
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:19.660
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.370
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:29.120
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.660
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.790
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.330
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.830
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:51.290
"Act 10"

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.790
Hiragi, sir!

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.830
Where's Otori?

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.250
We've looked all over the school,
but we can't find him!

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.370
You know where he is, don't you?

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.660
Apparently, Otori submitted
a leave of absence request.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.250
Leave of absence...?

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.250
Here is your new practice schedule

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.580
and your new stage assignment
for the Ayanagi Festival.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.040
Your performance has been moved
from the Ayanagi Grand Performance Hall

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.290
to the special outdoor stage.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.410
After all this time, we're getting
moved to the outdoor stage?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.870
The grand performance hall is
only for Star Teams, remember?

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.580
There's no helping it.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.370
The biggest problem is this.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:43.200
Our performance time
overlaps with Team Hiragi's.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.660
Most of the audience will probably
go to the grand performance hall.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.830
Don't you think he'll be back soon?

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:56.700
A leave of absence is usually
only about a week, right?

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.250
Even so, we're not a Star Team anymore.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.700
You have to face reality.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.160
That's cold.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:11.500
Nayuki and Hoshitani are both at a
loss <i>because</i> they're facing reality.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:16.200
Not everyone can be as
matter-of-fact as you, you boor!

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:20.580
I'm not satisfied with this, either, but if we
don't look forward, we can't start anything.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.540
The Ayanagi Festival is approaching fast.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.620
We don't have time!

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.120
Does that mean it's okay to ignore
Hoshitani and Nayuki's feelings?

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.000
Huh? When did I ignore them?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.330
Hey, calm down.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.950
How can I?!

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.330
Have you ever heard of the Scary Shumai?

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:44.540
There was once a man who bought
a box of ten <i>shumai</i> dumplings as a gift.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:48.500
When he opened the lid of
the box after passing a graveyard,

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.580
he saw that one was missing.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.000
He looked around, but no one was there.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.950
Thinking it was strange, he walked
for a while and opened the lid again,

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.790
and this time, two were missing.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.080
Every time he opened the lid,
another dumpling went missing,

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.830
until in the end, when he opened the lid--

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.580
They were all stuck to
the back of the lid, right?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.750
Want to make some <i>shumai</i> together?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:24.500
Mindlessly wrapping meat
will calm you down, you know...

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.330
No thanks.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.410
In any case, we decided
to look forward and continue.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:34.450
Sorry to make you wait!

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:35.330
You're late!

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.790
Sorry. I only just finished my
English homework from first period.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.950
Excuses can wait. Let's go!

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.870
Morning! I heard

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.870
that Otori suddenly took a
leave of absence from school.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.540
Must be hard.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.330
Oh... yeah...

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.200
You have a grain of rice on your back.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.250
Huh? No way...

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:17.500
After that, no one brought up Otori again.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.200
Morning.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.830
Oh, morning.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:32.290
I think everyone was worried.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.910
<i>Shumai</i> lunches today, too?

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.120
This is the fourth day in a row...

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.660
What? Do I hear complaining?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.120
Nope, I'm partaking gratefully.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.000
Do you think Nayuki's
personality's changed recently?

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.700
Like he's gotten stronger, or...

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.120
He's kind of scary.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.250
Did you say something?!

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.040
No!

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.660
Nothing!

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:23.500
But we were even stronger
and more cheerful than before.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.700
A star...

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.910
That does look like a star.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:37.450
Oh, that's our trademark!

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.330
You know, stardust!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.580
You mean how even though we're stardust,

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:44.700
if the five of us are gathered together,
we can give off a strong light?

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.830
The pointy parts of the star are the five of us!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:53.120
Then the green pea in the middle is Otor...

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.080
What lessons do we have in the afternoon?

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:12.330
Fifth period is a dance lesson
in Building 1, room 502.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:16.790
Sixth period is a chorus lesson
in Building 3, room 201.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.370
We have to go from one end of
the school to the other again, huh?

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.870
It's really annoying being a regular team.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:30.450
I felt like if I didn't hide
the uneasiness in my heart,

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.290
the five of us would drift apart.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:44.330
Tengenji, how do you feel about
performing with your father for the first time?

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.080
I am honored.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.370
However, as actors, we are rivals.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:53.790
In the movie, I hope to challenge him head on.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:00.660
Tengenji, you look really cool like this!

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.040
Look at this! And this, and this!

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.250
"Kakeru Tengenji"
"Movie Way"

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.410
"Tokyo Age"

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.620
Tengenji's on all the covers!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.660
No, Tavian.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.410
It's just a small part. Everyone's
making too big a deal about it.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:18.330
I can't refuse either 'cause
the old man's asking me to do it.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.330
Looks like you'll be busy.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.080
Will you be able to come to school?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.450
Yeah, that part's fine. It's just...

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.950
Tengenji said he has filming in the afternoons,

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:37.700
so he won't be able
to come to practice for a while.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:39.120
I see.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.910
I would also like to take
a break from our practices.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.200
You too, Tsukigami?

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.830
There's an audition for the ensemble
for a musical I've been wanting to be in.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.540
I want to try auditioning even
though I don't think I'll get it.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.450
What a great chance!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.160
Of course, we're rooting for you!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.870
Sorry...

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.370
Don't worry about it!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.120
It's just the two of us again, huh?

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.040
It's kind of lonely...

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.910
It can't be helped.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:19.040
Kuga can't take off from
work on Sundays, either.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.290
Everyone's amazing, huh?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.080
Even with everything that's going on,
they're still looking forward and working hard.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.290
All right!

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:39.450
I've decided!

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:41.830
Huh?

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.160
Come on! Let's go!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.950
Wait, Hoshitani!

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.250
Where are you planning on going?

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:07.660
Well, ever since school started,
we've just been practicing.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.700
We haven't done anything fun!

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:12.700
I thought it'd be nice
to go out together sometime.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:16.830
That's fine, but I don't
know this area very well.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:18.950
I don't either!

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:20.080
Don't worry!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.370
Ta-da! Look what I brought!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.500
"A Cool Guy's Guide to Walking Around Town"?

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:31.000
If we follow this guide, we'll be cool, too!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.120
Probably!

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.120
Over here, Nayuki!

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.950
The people look like sesame seeds!

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:50.080
Hoshitani, is it your first time
being somewhere so high?

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.200
Yeah!

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.950
It's so wide!

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:58.580
Oh, that's cute!

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.330
So fast!

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.410
"Fresh Fizzy Lemonade" "Citric acid! Vitamin!!" "Charge!"

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.410
Delish!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.500
Um, Hoshitani...

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.160
Oh, Nayuki, you're not having fun?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.750
I am, but...

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.910
Good!

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:21.910
Let's see... The next recommended spot is...

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.660
Hoshitani, can I see that page?

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.290
Huh? Sure...

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.040
I knew it...

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.370
Hm?

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.040
This says it's a date course for couples.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.200
Huh?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:50.450
I thought it was kind of weird when it
started feeling like a date halfway through.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.120
Jeez, say something then!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.700
I feel kind of hungry now after laughing.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.700
"Chinatown"

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.660
I'm so full!

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.290
That was good!

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:13.250
Will we be all right?
I don't have much money on me.

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:16.910
Leave it to me. It'll be my treat!

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:20.660
Wait, I don't have my wallet...

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.040
What?

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.870
Did you drop it somewhere?

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.290
That's weird...

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:26.700
Found you!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.250
Wh-What's with this giant <i>shumai</i> ?!

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:39.250
♪ If you're hungry,
come to the Bow-Wow House ♪

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:43.080
♪ Everyone's smiling at the Bow-Wow House ♪

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.160
Help!

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:46.830
♪ Bow-Wow House ♪

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.750
Cut!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.830
Break for ten minutes!

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:00.330
"Hoshitani: Oh noooooo!
What should we do? This is bad~ (&gt;O&lt;)"

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:10.830
"Bow-Wow House"

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.410
Bow-Wow House. This is it!

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.370
Are you all right, Hoshitani? Nayuki?!

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:20.790
What?

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:25.870
Oh, Tengenji!

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.450
Tsukigami and Kuga, too...

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.870
Tengenji, what about filming for the movie?

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:35.120
I did everything in one take
to finish quickly so I could come!

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.910
What's with those clothes?

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:40.080
Actually...

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.580
Let me explain!

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:46.370
I'm the singing and dancing son
of the Bow-Wow House--

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:50.120
Seishiro Inumine!

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.450
That's me!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.660
Why is Team Hiragi here?

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:57.580
'Cause this is my family's restaurant.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.950
We were supposed to
wear these <i>shumai</i> outfits...

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:05.540
Of Bow-Wow House's
mascot idol, Shumai Dog!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:09.330
...and perform in the
restaurant's event tonight.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:14.080
But Toraishi and Ugawa
ran away after seeing these outfits.

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.500
Not surprising.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.700
Just as I was thinking, "Oh no, what'll we do?"

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:23.410
I happened to spot Hoshitani and Nayuki!

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:28.120
Is this chance? No, it's fate.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.750
You came all this way.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.120
We'll let you guys play these parts.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.410
No thanks! Who would do that?

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.410
It's fate!

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:38.160
Let's dance and sing together!

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:35.830
Actually, I lent Hoshitani and Nayuki money to pay for their meal.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:39.790
The performance fee will cancel out their debt.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.660
"Mr. Eigo Sawatari"
"We have received the above mentioned."

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:44.410
Let's dance and sing together!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.830
♪ If you're hungry,
come to the Bow-Wow House ♪

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:56.700
♪ Everyone's smiling at the Bow-Wow House ♪

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.790
♪ Bow-Wow House ♪

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.700
♪ Bow-Wow House ♪

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:04.750
♪ Meat-filled <i>shumai</i> filled with meat juices ♪

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:08.500
♪ Shrimp <i>shumai</i> filled with lots of shrimp ♪

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:09.910
♪ Bow-Wow... ♪

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.000
Hoshitani...!

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.950
I'm sorry!

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.160
That was fun!

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.790
No, it wasn't!

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.080
What if a fan saw me?!

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:31.830
My cool image will go down the drain!

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:34.750
But you looked like you were having fun.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.660
Shut up!

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:40.870
If Otori was there, everyone would
have had even more fun, though.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.040
Yeah, he likes to goof around.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:46.620
"Now, boys! It's time to play!"

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:49.410
That's what he'd say, I'm sure.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:55.910
I want to hear him call us "boys" again.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:59.660
I don't think I can do
my best without hearing that.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.080
Huh...?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.500
What's wrong?

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:06.370
I thought talking about Otori was taboo.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.540
Taboo?

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:11.160
Everyone seemed to be avoiding it.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.540
Oh yeah.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.660
Hoshitani, you like Otori, don't you?

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:25.700
We didn't want to talk about Otori
and make you remember him.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:30.080
Oh, was that what it was?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.000
Tengenji, you are like a beautiful flower.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.040
Try letting that flower bloom bigger.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.700
Be aware of the audience.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.910
Kuga, you have good rhythm.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:56.450
Sharpen all your nerves and become the music.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.870
Don't think you don't have
any distinguishing characteristics.

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:02.080
You're good at everything,
and that's your greatest strength.

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.910
Just perform like yourself, Tsukigami.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:08.410
Nayuki, your weapon is your sensitivity.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:11.910
People's joy, anger, sadness...

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:14.870
Try expressing them just as you feel them.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:19.500
Hoshitani, push straight on forward!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.620
Make the world lose
themselves in your performance!

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.750
I felt like the five of us were drifting apart,

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.580
but that was a groundless fear.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:41.160
Well, since the five of us
are together, let's practice!

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.910
What? Right now?

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:47.450
Of course. In order for a
regular team to get to the top,

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:51.370
we have to practice ten times
more than those Star Team guys.

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:53.040
Especially you, Hoshitani!

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:58.450
I'm going to work you hard
in Otori's place, so get ready!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.620
What do you say?

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.660
Y-Yes, sir!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.410
All right!

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:26.500
♪ Shiny... ♪

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.450
♪ Stardust... ♪

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:55.000
♪ If this light was by itself ♪

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:59.410
♪ It might have been scattered ♪

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:03.950
♪ This small light ♪

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:09.410
♪ If I was alone ♪

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:13.790
♪ I might've hesitated and looked downcast ♪

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:19.450
♪ That's what it seems like to me ♪

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.790
♪ If we're together ♪

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:26.950
♪ We can make our dreams come true ♪

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:30.790
♪ Formation! Move forward! ♪

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:36.540
♪ Five stars moving together in a line ♪

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.580
♪ Do the Dancin' ♪

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:41.370
♪ Sparking passion ♪

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:45.370
♪ Stretch out your hand if you want it ♪

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:51.910
♪ You smile brightest when
you're too absorbed in something! ♪

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:59.540
♪ A voice somewhere says, "Have fun, boys!" ♪

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:03.160
♪ It's so bright I can't see ♪

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.000
♪ But I'm not afraid ♪

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:12.450
♪ Look, the intro's starting! ♪

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.370
Here's Otori's email address.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:37.700
I got it from Hiragi.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:40.910
You haven't talked to Otori yet, have you?

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:44.370
Thanks.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.620
"from: Yuta Hoshitani"
"to: Otori"

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:55.120
"We..."
"Send | Save | Delete"

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:02.870
I want to know, after all.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:06.540
You boys are fine the way you are.

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:09.950
Do your best. Make sure you don't lose, boys!

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:17.120
Otori, why did you leave us?

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:38.830
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:45.330
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:48.830
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:53.120
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:57.250
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:57.250 --> 00:23:00.500
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:04.080
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:08.080
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:11.250
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:23:11.250 --> 00:23:15.120
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.620
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:22.370
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:25.910
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:29.580
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:35.580
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:55.950
"King Edward"

00:23:56.370 --> 00:24:20.830
"Act 11"

00:23:56.790 --> 00:23:59.330
Sawatari! Sawatari! This CD's weird!

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:01.870
It won't play even after
I put it in the CD player!

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:05.330
What if it's some other kind
of disc and not a CD?

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:07.620
I wouldn't be surprised if you made
a mistake because they're the same shape.

00:24:07.620 --> 00:24:09.950
Oh, you're right! It was a donut!

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:10.950
Do-not...!

00:24:11.120 --> 00:24:20.830
"There's no way you can miss it! Right, Tatsumin?♥︎"
"Hiragi"
